  "limits": "A container codec only: it checks the header, the chunk layout and the binding of buffers[0] to the BIN chunk, not the glTF document inside (accessors, meshes and references are left to a document validator). The returned binary is a view into the input, so changing the input changes it. Chunks of unknown types after the first two are listed and skipped, as the specification asks; their contents are not read. Writing keeps the JSON as JSON.stringify gives it. Only the Node 22 tests and three.js 0.186.1 GLTFExporter and GLTFLoader in headless Chrome were run.",
